The shaded region between $y=3x$ and the $y$-axis from $y=0$ to $y=6$ is rotated about the $y$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1cm, y=0.75cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:6, samples=2, variable=\y] ({\y/3},{\y}) -- (0,6) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-2.8,0) -- (2.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.4) -- (0,7.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-0.8:2.4, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*\x}) node[pos=0.98, right] {$y=3x$};
\node[left] at (0,6) {$6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region between $y=x^{2}$ and the $y$-axis from $y=0$ to $y=7$ is rotated about the $y$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1cm, y=0.6cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:7, samples=60, variable=\y] ({sqrt(\y)},{\y}) -- (0,7) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3.2,0) -- (3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.8) -- (0,9.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-2.9:2.9, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x}) node[pos=0.98, right] {$y=x^{2}$};
\node[left] at (0,7) {$7$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region between $y=x^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from $y=0$ to $y=1$ is rotated about the $y$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.8cm, y=1.8cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:1, samples=60, variable=\y] ({pow(\y,0.3333)},{\y}) -- (0,1) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.6,0) -- (1.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.8) -- (0,1.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.15:1.15, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x*\x}) node[pos=0.98, right] {$y=x^{3}$};
\node[left] at (0,1) {$1$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region between $y=x-2$ and the $y$-axis from $y=0$ to $y=4$ is rotated about the $y$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.75cm, y=0.75cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:4, samples=2, variable=\y] ({\y+2},{\y}) -- (0,4) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.6,0) -- (7.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.4) -- (0,5.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1:7, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x-2}) node[pos=0.98, below right] {$y=x-2$};
\node[left] at (0,4) {$4$};
\node[below] at (2,-0.25) {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region between $y=9-x^{2}$ and the $y$-axis from $y=0$ to $y=5$ is rotated about the $y$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.75cm, y=0.45cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:5, samples=60, variable=\y] ({sqrt(9-\y)},{\y}) -- (0,5) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-4.2,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.4) -- (0,11.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-3.35:3.35, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{9-\x*\x}) node[pos=0.40, above left] {$y=9-x^{2}$};
\node[left] at (0,5) {$5$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The shaded region lies between $y=2\sqrt{x}$ and the $y$-axis, from the origin to the point on the curve where $x=4$.
It is rotated about the $y$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.85cm, y=1.1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:4, samples=60, variable=\y] ({\y*\y/4},{\y}) -- (0,4) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.4,0) -- (6.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1) -- (0,5.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, ->, domain=0:6, samples=80, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2*sqrt(\x)}) node[pos=0.98, above right] {$y=2\sqrt{x}$};
\fill (4,4) circle (0.07);
\node[above left] at (4,4) {$(4,4)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region between $y=2x$ and the $y$-axis from $y=0$ to $y=k$, where $k>0$, is rotated about the $y$-axis.
The solid has volume $144\pi\ \text{units}^{3}$.
Find $k$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.6cm, y=0.4cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:10, samples=2, variable=\y] ({\y/2},{\y}) -- (0,10) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-5.2,0) -- (5.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-4.4) -- (0,13.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-2.2:5, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2*\x}) node[pos=0.98, right] {$y=2x$};
\node[left] at (0,10) {$k$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
